p` | `fopen` fails, `ENOENT`: path does not exist | `stderr` `\"Error: opening or processing file <path>\\n\"`, no `fclose` (fp is NULL), returns `NULL` | [x] |\n| 5 | `open_with_cleanup` | `fopen` fails, `ENOENT`: empty string path `\"\"` | as row 4 with `<path>` empty | [x] |\n| 6 | `open_with_cleanup` | `filename == NULL` (null pointer across FFI) | `fopen(NULL,\"r\")` → `NULL`; `fprintf(\"%s\", NULL)` prints `(null)`; returns `NULL` | [x] |\n| 7 | `open_with_cleanup` | `fopen` fails, `EACCES`: existing file with mode `000` | as row 4, returns `NULL` | [x] |\n| 8 | `open_with_cleanup` | `fopen` fails, `ENAMETOOLONG`: oversized path (~5000 bytes, > `PATH_MAX`) | as row 4 (whole oversized name echoed to stderr), returns `NULL` | [x] |\n| 9 | `open_with_cleanup` | `fopen` fails, `ENOTDIR`: a regular file used as a directory component | as row 4, returns `NULL` | [x] |\n|10 | `open_with_cleanup` | `fopen` *succeeds* but the read loop sets `ferror` (`EISDIR`: path is a directory) | takes the second `goto cleanup`: stderr message, **`fclose(fp)` is executed**, returns `NULL` | [x] |\n|11 | `driver` | `forward_goto_example` returned `-1` (`num < 0`) → early `return -1`; the file is never opened | returns `-1`, stderr has only the negative-input message, `stdout` empty, no file error message | [x] |\n|12 | `driver` | `num < 0` **and** a bad filename (error precedence: first error wins) | returns `-1` (not `-2`); no `\"opening or processing\"` message at all | [x] |\n|13 | `driver` | `num >= 0`, `open_with_cleanup` returned `NULL` (all of rows 4–10 as filenames) | returns `-2` after printing `Processing:`/`Goto output:` | [x] |\n|14 | `driver` | `num = INT_MIN` (extreme, negative) / `num = INT_MAX` (extreme, positive, `x*2` overflows) with a bad file | `INT_MIN` → `-1`; `INT_MAX` → `-2` (overflowed `res = -2` is *not* the `-1` sentinel) | [x] |\n|15 | `driver` | `filename == NULL` with `num >= 0` | returns `-2`, stderr contains `(null)` | [x] |\n|16 | `open_with_cleanup` 