{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fzuofat6uyixwsnqyvvakpdqgoaw3uvgvlcsjx33zsqfpo26ugna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Summary:\n\n## Result: the Rust translation is byte-identical to the C — no divergences found\n\n**Scope.** The library is one translation unit (`c_src/src/goto.c`, 81 lines) exporting 3 symbols. `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`** and `CMakeLists.txt` has no options/`#ifdef` variants, so there is exactly one build configuration; all three equivalent cargo invocations (`default`, `--no-default-features`, `--all-features`) plus the `release` profile are run by `./verify.sh`.\n\n**Phase A — artifacts** (all derived mechanically from the C source):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 3/3 C symbols exported by the Rust `.so`, `nm -D` diff empty, nothing untranslated (no skipped module → no stubs needed).\n- `ERRORS.md` — 19 rows from every `goto error`/`goto cleanup`/`return -1`/`return -2` site, including the `fopen`-failure sub-cases (ENOENT/EACCES/ENAMETOOLONG/ENOTDIR/NULL/empty path) and the *second* `goto cleanup` (`ferror` after `fopen` on a directory succeeds).\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 26 rows over the axes the C actually branches on: `int` value class (incl. `x*2` overflow), file shape (empty/1/many lines, exact `fgets(…,100)` boundaries, embedded NULs, binary, 80 KiB, `/dev/null`, non-UTF-8 names), stream topology (separate vs. **same fd**, so stdout/stderr interleaving is diffed), and call sequencing.\n\n**Phases B–C — differential tests** (`tests/`, 55 tests): both `.so`s are `dlopen`ed and called only through their exported symbols. Compared per call: return value, the exact bytes on fd 1 *and* fd 2 (via `dup2` capture), the state of the returned `FILE*` (`ferror`/`feof`/`ftell`/`fgetc`/`fclose`), and `/proc/self/fd` deltas — the only way to observe the C's `fclose` calls.\n\n**Two harness bugs I found and fixed** (they would have made the whole exercise vacuous):\n